  "candidate_0019": {
    "reason": "The assertion conflates a common implementation with a necessary condition. While RAG often involves retrieval, alternative implementations exist (e.g., using pre-fetched knowledge bases or internal vector stores without external document fetching) that still constitute RAG. The literal claim implies an absolute requirement for 'retrieving relevant external documents,' which is not strictly true; ","counterexample": "A system performing Retrieval Augmented Generation by querying a local, static vector database of internal company manuals without accessing any external documents.","sound_as_stated": false
  }
